export default {"id":"sounddesign-level-13","number":13,"title":"Edm Genre Labs","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Master the acoustic DNA of modern Dubstep & Bass Music (140-150 BPM half-time, sub dominance from 30-80 Hz, vocal formant growls, syncopated riddim wubs). - Synthesize all primary bass archetypes from scratch:","modules":[{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-1-1","code":"13.1","title":"Dubstep / Bass Music Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic DNA of modern Dubstep & Bass Music (140-150 BPM half-time, sub dominance from 30-80 Hz, vocal formant growls, syncopated riddim wubs). - Synthesize all primary bass archetypes from scratch:","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-53","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic DNA of modern <strong>Dubstep &amp; Bass Music</strong> (140-150 BPM half-time, sub dominance from 30-80 Hz, vocal formant growls, syncopated riddim wubs).","Synthesize all primary bass archetypes from scratch:","<strong>Syncopated Wub Bass</strong> (<code>Surge XT</code> / <code>Vital</code>)","<strong>Vocal Formant Growl</strong> (<code>Vital</code> Formant Scale + Multiband OTT)","<strong>Aggressive FM Cascaded Growl</strong> (<code>Operator</code> Algorithm 1 + Pitch Env)","<strong>Metallic Laser Screech</strong> (<code>Vital</code> Hard Sync + Comb Filter)","Implement strict <strong>Sub Layer Separation</strong> (100 Hz crossover, pure mono sine sub).","Build a multi-bass <strong>Call-and-Response Drop Sequence</strong> across a 2-bar grid.","Assemble and macro-map an 8-knob Dubstep Performance Rack for the Novation Launchkey MK4."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-1","title":"13.1.1 — Dubstep Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.1 — Dubstep Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Dubstep is defined by half-time rhythmic weight (140-150 BPM, kick on Beat 1, snare on Beat 3) and high-density, dynamically evolving basslines:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                  DUBSTEP ACOUSTIC FREQUENCY MATRIX                                |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| FREQUENCY BAND    | ACOUSTIC ROLE               | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | PROCESSING PROTOCOL     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$30 - 80\\text{ Hz}$**| **Sub-Bass Fundamental**    | `Drift` / `Operator`  | **100% Pure Mono Sine** |\n|                   | (Massive club chest impact) | (Clean single sine)   | Zero Distortion / No FX |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$100\\text{ Hz}-2\\text{ kHz}$**| **Mid-Range Growl / Wub**   | `Vital` / `Surge XT`  | Heavy Multi-Stage Drive,|\n|                   | (Vocal formant / FM grit)   | (Formant / FM3 / K35) | Multiband OTT Dynamics  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$&gt;2\\text{ kHz}$**| **Transient Sizzle &amp; Noise**| Noise / Wavetable Air | Stereo Chorus / Flanger,|\n|                   | (Cutting bite &amp; presence)   | (Sync / Phase Warp)   | Short Plate Reverb      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §2 &amp; §6","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-2","title":"13.1.2 — The Syncopated Wobble / Wub Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.2 — The Syncopated Wobble / Wub Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: SYNCOPATED DUBSTEP WUB                                   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Surge XT** (or Vital)                                |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Algorithm: **Classic**, Shape: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **-1**|\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Algorithm: **Modern**, Shape: **Square**, Oct: **-1**, Level: **-3 dB**|\n| **FILTER 1**         | Model: **Vintage K35 (LP18)**, Cutoff: **160 Hz**, Res: **0.75**|\n| **WAVESHAPER**       | Model: **Asymmetric**, Drive: **+10 dB**               |\n| **MODULATION**       | **Voice LFO 1:** Shape: **Sine**, Rate: **1/8th Note Sync**|\n|                      | - Route LFO 1 to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+85%)**            |\n|                      | - Route LFO 1 to **Waveshaper Drive (+35%)**           |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> The MS-20 resonant peak screaming into the asymmetrical waveshaper creates the signature aggressive mid-tempo wobble."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §6.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-3","title":"13.1.3 — The Vocal / Formant Growl","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.3 — The Vocal / Formant Growl","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: VOCAL FORMANT GROWL                                      |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Warp: **Formant Scale** |\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Dirty LP24**, Cutoff: **180 Hz**, Res: **0.45**|\n| **MODULATION**       | **LFO 1:** Mode **Trigger**, Rate **1/4th Sync**       |\n|                      | - Draw custom multi-peak Bezier formant curve          |\n|                      | - Route LFO 1 to **Formant Scale Warp (+70%)**         |\n|                      | - Route LFO 1 to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+65%)**            |\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Distortion:** Mode **Soft Clip**, Drive **+12 dB** |\n|                      | 2. **Compressor:** Mode **Multiband (OTT)**, Mix **80%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> As LFO 1 sweeps the Formant Scale warp, the sound transforms into an unmistakable, snarling \"Yoi-Yoi\" dubstep monster growl."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 2.5 &amp; 7.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-4","title":"13.1.4 — The Cascaded FM Growl","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.4 — The Cascaded FM Growl","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: CASCADED OPERATOR FM GROWL                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 1** (Cascaded Stack: D -&gt; C -&gt; B -&gt; A)     |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Wave: **Saw D**, Coarse: **1**, Level: **0.0 dB** (Carrier)|\n| **OPERATOR B**       | Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1**, Level: **-8.0 dB**      |\n| **OPERATOR C**       | Wave: **4-Sine**, Coarse: **2**, Level: **-12.0 dB**   |\n| **OPERATOR D**       | Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1**, Feedback: **65%**, Level: **-6.0 dB**|\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Pitch Env ON for **Osc D Only**, Amount: **+36 st**, Decay: **85 ms**|\n| **FILTER &amp; DRIVE**   | Mode: **Band-Pass BP24**, Cutoff: **1.2 kHz**, Drive: **PRD (+8 dB)**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A tearing, metallic FM growl seed driven by pitch-swept feedback and saturated bandpass filtering."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 23 (Operator)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-5","title":"13.1.5 — Sub-Bass Layer Separation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.5 — Sub-Bass Layer Separation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"In professional dubstep production, <strong>the mid growl synth must NEVER output sub-bass</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ MID GROWL TRACK (Vital / Surge) ] ===&gt; [ HIGH-PASS FILTER (HP48 @ 100 Hz) ] ===&gt; Audio Out\n                                                                                       +\n[ DEDICATED SUB TRACK (Operator)   ] ===&gt; [ PURE SINE @ 0 dB ] ===&gt; [ UTILITY: MONO ] ===&gt; Audio Out\n                                          (Zero Distortion, Zero FX)</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Insert an <code>EQ Eight</code> on your Mid Growl track and apply a steep 48 dB/oct High-Pass cut at <strong>100 Hz</strong>.","Create a dedicated MIDI track loaded with <code>Operator</code> (Algorithm 11, single Sine oscillator, pitch tracking).","Copy the MIDI baseline to both tracks.","The sub remains 100% clean and phase-coherent, while the mid growl is free to undergo violent distortion and stereo widening."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §6.1"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-6","title":"13.1.6 — The Mid-Bass Processing Chain","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.6 — The Mid-Bass Processing Chain","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ MID GROWL OUTPUT ] ===&gt; [ EQ EIGHT (HP @ 100 Hz, 350 Hz Mud Notch) ]\n                     ===&gt; [ SATURATOR (Drive +4 dB, Analog Clip) ]\n                     ===&gt; [ MULTIBAND DYNAMICS (OTT Compression: Upward +6 dB) ]\n                     ===&gt; [ CHORUS-ENSEMBLE (Highs Only &gt; 2.5 kHz) ]\n                     ===&gt; [ UTILITY (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz) ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-7","title":"13.1.7 — Call-and-Response Drop Structure","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.7 — Call-and-Response Drop Structure","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A compelling dubstep drop never repeats one single bass patch continuously. It arranges distinct sound designs into a <strong>2-Bar Conversation</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">2-BAR DROP GRID:\nBar 1, Beat 1-2: [ BASS A: Monster Vocal Growl (\"YOI-YOI\") ] ===&gt; (The Call)\nBar 1, Beat 3-4: [ BASS B: Fast 1/16th Riddim Wub ]          ===&gt; (The Response)\nBar 2, Beat 1-2: [ BASS C: Metallic Laser Screech ]          ===&gt; (The Variation)\nBar 2, Beat 3-4: [ BASS D: Resampled Reversed Bass Drop ]     ===&gt; (The Turnaround)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-8","title":"13.1.8 — Screech / Laser Lead","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.8 — Screech / Laser Lead","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: DUBSTEP LASER SCREECH                                    |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Warp: **Sync**          |\n| **ENVELOPE 2**       | Attack: **0 ms**, Decay: **90 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**    |\n|                      | - Route Env 2 to **Osc 1 Pitch (+36 st)** (Instant Drop)|\n|                      | - Route Env 2 to **Sync Warp (+80%)**                  |\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Comb+**, Cutoff: **2.4 kHz**, Feedback: **75%**|\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | **Delay:** Mode **Ping-Pong**, Sync **1/16th**, Mix **30%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 2 &amp; 4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-9","title":"13.1.9 — Synthetic Metallic Dubstep Snare","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.9 — Synthetic Metallic Dubstep Snare","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: SYNTHETIC DUBSTEP SNARE (200 Hz Body + Noise Snap)      |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 4**                                        |\n| **OSC A (Body)**     | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1** (200 Hz)|\n|                      | Pitch Env: **+18 st**, Pitch Decay: **35 ms**          |\n| **OSC C (Snap)**     | Mode: **Fixed (8.5 kHz)**, Wave: **Noise White**       |\n|                      | AEG Decay: **220 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**                |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Dynamic Tube` (Drive +4 dB) -&gt; `Glue Compressor` (Fast)|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §6.4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-10","title":"13.1.10 — Resampling Workflow for Bass Stems","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.10 — Resampling Workflow for Bass Stems","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Render 8 bars of evolving growl modulation onto an audio track (<code>Freeze &amp; Flatten</code>).","Set the Live 12 grid to <strong>16th Notes</strong>.","Use <strong><code>Ctrl + E</code></strong> to slice the audio at every transient.","Select every 4th slice and hit <strong><code>R</code></strong> to reverse it into a rising swell.","Transpose select slices down -3 st or -5 st to construct complex melodic variations."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §6.3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-11","title":"13.1.11 — Dubstep Macro Performance Template","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.11 — Dubstep Macro Performance Template","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        DUBSTEP LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                            |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Growl Formant Sweep / Vowel Morph**                     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **Wub Modulation Rate (1/4 -&gt; 1/8 -&gt; 1/16)**              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Filter Cutoff / Screech Open**                          |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Distortion Drive Amount**                               |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **OTT Multiband Crunch Depth**                            |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Comb Filter Resonance / Metallic Grit**                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Stereo Chorus / Width on Highs**                        |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master Reverb Splash / Space Swell**                    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-1-12","title":"13.1.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 4-Element Drop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.1.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 4-Element Drop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Program a half-time drum beat at 140 BPM (Kick on 1, Snare on 3).","Insert a dedicated Sub Bass track with <code>Operator</code> (clean sine, mono).","Insert three mid-bass tracks (<code>Vital</code> Formant Growl, <code>Surge XT</code> K35 Wub, <code>Vital</code> Laser Screech).","Construct a 2-bar call-and-response phrase where the three mid patches alternate every 2 beats over the locked sub foundation.","Export your final drop stem to your User Library as <code>SD_Lab_DubstepDrop_140BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-2-2","code":"13.2","title":"Drum & Bass Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic architecture of Drum & Bass (170-176 BPM, 2-step breakbeats, sub weight, and Reese bass evolution). - Synthesize the definitive DnB bass archetypes:","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-54","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic architecture of <strong>Drum &amp; Bass</strong> (170-176 BPM, 2-step breakbeats, sub weight, and Reese bass evolution).","Synthesize the definitive DnB bass archetypes:","<strong>The Classic 1995 Reese Bass</strong> (Detuned analog saws + LPF)","<strong>The Modern Neurofunk Reese</strong> (Multi-band notch sweeps + Serial distortion)","<strong>The Roller Foghorn Bass</strong> (Saturated low-passed FM punch)","<strong>Liquid DnB Atmospheric Pad</strong> (Evolving wavetable bed)","Synthesize a punchy 174 BPM Kick and 200 Hz Snare transient.","Execute the <strong>Neurofunk Resampling Loop</strong> in Ableton Live 12.","Build a complete 174 BPM Drum &amp; Bass drop from scratch."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-1","title":"13.2.1 — Drum & Bass Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.1 — Drum & Bass Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Drum &amp; Bass is engineered for extreme club sound system impact at high tempos (170-176 BPM):"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                     DNB FREQUENCY TOPOLOGY                                        |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| FREQUENCY BAND    | ACOUSTIC ROLE               | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | PROCESSING BEHAVIOR     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$35 - 75\\text{ Hz}$**| **Sub-Bass Fundamental**    | `Drift` / `Operator`  | **Strict Mono Sine**,   |\n|                   | (Massive, immovable root)   | (Single clean sine)   | Locked phase, zero mod. |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$100\\text{ Hz}-1\\text{ kHz}$**| **Mid-Bass Movement (Reese)**| `Surge XT` / `Vital`  | Heavy saturation,       |\n|                   | (Phase beating / notch sweeps) (Detuned Saws / Tables)| automated notch filters|\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$&gt;3\\text{ kHz}$**| **Transient Air &amp; Breakbeats**| `Simpler` / Break Slices| Crisp stereo presence, |\n|                   | (Snare crack &amp; hi-hat shuffle)| (Amen / Think breaks) | High-pass filtered.     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §2 &amp; §6","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-2","title":"13.2.2 — The Classic Reese Bass (Kevin 'Reese' Saunderson Legacy)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.2 — The Classic Reese Bass (Kevin 'Reese' Saunderson Legacy)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Originating from Kevin Saunderson's 1988 track <em>\"Just Want Another Chance\"</em> (under the alias <strong>Reese</strong>), the Reese bass is created by two detuned sawtooth waves beating against each other:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ OSC 1: SAWTOOTH @ 55 Hz (A1) ] ---+\n                                    |===&gt; [ LOW-PASS FILTER (LP24 @ 450 Hz) ] ===&gt; [ SATURATOR ]\n[ OSC 2: SAWTOOTH @ 55.6 Hz (+18c) ]-+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: CLASSIC 1995 REESE BASS                                  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Surge XT** (Classic Engine) or **Drift**             |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Wave: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **-1**, Detune: **-10 cents** |\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Wave: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **-1**, Detune: **+10 cents** |\n|                      | (Total 20-cent detune creates a 0.6 Hz phase beating cycle)|\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Ladder LP24**, Cutoff: **420 Hz**, Res: **0.20**|\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Saturator` (Soft Sine, Drive +5 dB) -&gt; `Utility` (Mono)|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A warm, menacing, rolling analog bass with organic low-frequency phase beating."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §6.2 (The Classic Reese Path)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-3","title":"13.2.3 — The Modern Neurofunk Reese","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.3 — The Modern Neurofunk Reese","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Modern neurofunk expands on the classic Reese by splitting the mid-range and carving moving spectral notches through distortion circuits:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: MODERN NEUROFUNK REESE                                  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Unison: **6 Voices**    |\n|                      | Detune: **14%**, Warp: **Harmonic Stretch (30%)**      |\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Notch 24 dB**, Cutoff: **650 Hz**, Res: **0.70**|\n| **MODULATION**       | **LFO 1:** Mode **Sync**, Rate **1/2 Bar**, Shape **Tri**|\n|                      | Route LFO 1 to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+60%)** (Sweeping notch)|\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Distortion:** Mode **Sine Fold**, Drive **+10 dB** |\n|                      | 2. **Compressor:** Mode **Multiband (OTT)**, Mix **75%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A snarling, phased, mechanical neurofunk bass with sweeping spectral valleys and wave-folded distortion harmonics."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §6.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-4","title":"13.2.4 — The Roller Foghorn Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.4 — The Roller Foghorn Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The definitive sound of modern DnB \"rollers\":"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: DNB ROLLER FOGHORN                                       |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 1**                                        |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1**, Level: **0.0 dB**|\n| **OPERATOR B**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1**, Level: **-8.0 dB**|\n| **OPERATOR C**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Square D**, Coarse: **2**, Level: **-14 dB**|\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **Low-Pass LP24**, Cutoff: **380 Hz**, Drive: **OSR (+6 dB)**|\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Amount: **+12 st**, Decay: **45 ms** (Fast transient drop)|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> An immense, room-filling low-mid horn blast that punches on the downbeat and rolls smoothly across 16th-note basslines."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §6.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-5","title":"13.2.5 — Sub-Bass Separation for DnB","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.5 — Sub-Bass Separation for DnB","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"At 174 BPM, bass notes fire at rapid speed. Any phase cancellation in the sub-bass results in immediate low-end volume dropout on club sound systems:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ NEURO / REESE MID TRACK ] ===&gt; [ HIGH-PASS FILTER (HP48 @ 100 Hz) ] ===&gt; (Mid Processing)\n                                                                                  +\n[ CLEAN SUB TRACK         ] ===&gt; [ OPERATOR SINE (A1 = 55 Hz) ] ===&gt; [ UTILITY: MONO ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Rule:</strong> Always high-pass your Reese and Foghorn mid-basses at 100 Hz, letting a dedicated monophonic Sine sub track carry the foundational low-end weight."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-6","title":"13.2.6 — Mid-Bass Processing Chain","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.6 — Mid-Bass Processing Chain","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ REESE MID TRACK ] ===&gt; [ EQ EIGHT (HP 100 Hz, 300 Hz Notch) ]\n                    ===&gt; [ SATURATOR (Drive +5 dB) ]\n                    ===&gt; [ AUTO FILTER (Sweeping Band-Pass LFO) ]\n                    ===&gt; [ GLUE COMPRESSOR (Attack 30 ms, Release Fast) ]\n                    ===&gt; [ UTILITY (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz) ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §8"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-7","title":"13.2.7 — Synthesizing 174 BPM Drum & Bass Drums","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.7 — Synthesizing 174 BPM Drum & Bass Drums","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| SYNTHETIC 174 BPM KICK DRUM:                                                  |\n| - Engine: `Operator` (Single Sine, Pitch Env: +36 st -&gt; 50 Hz in 38 ms)       |\n| - Fast, tight, sub-heavy transient engineered not to clash with fast snares.  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| SYNTHETIC 200 HZ DNB SNARE:                                                   |\n| - Engine: `Operator` (Osc A: 200 Hz Tonal Body; Osc C: Noise Wires)           |\n| - High-Pass Filter @ 150 Hz, `Dynamic Tube` Drive for crisp high-end snap.    |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-8","title":"13.2.8 — The Neuro Resampling Loop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.8 — The Neuro Resampling Loop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ 1. PLAY 4 BARS OF REESE BASS ] ===&gt; [ 2. RECORD TO AUDIO (FREEZE &amp; FLATTEN) ]\n                                                        |\n                                                        v\n                                      [ 3. SLICE AT TRANSIENTS &amp; REVERSE SLICES ]\n                                                        |\n                                                        v\n                                      [ 4. INSERT FLANGER &amp; RE-FILTER ]\n                                                        |\n                                                        v\n                                      [ 5. RE-RENDER TO FINAL STEM ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §6.3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-9","title":"13.2.9 — Vocal Chop Design for Jungle / Liquid DnB","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.9 — Vocal Chop Design for Jungle / Liquid DnB","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Load an R&amp;B vocal snippet into <code>Simpler</code> in <strong>Slicing Mode</strong>.","Set Slice Mode to <strong>Transient</strong> with sensitivity at 65%.","Set Warp Mode to <strong>Complex Pro</strong> (Preserves natural vocal formants).","Transpose pitch up <strong>+5 or +7 semitones</strong>.","Trigger vocal slices via MIDI pads in sync with 174 BPM rolling breakbeats."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-10","title":"13.2.10 — Atmospheric Pads for Liquid DnB","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.10 — Atmospheric Pads for Liquid DnB","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: LIQUID DNB CINEMATIC PAD                                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital** (or Surge XT)                                |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Vocal / Strings**, Unison: **8 Voices**       |\n|                      | Detune: **12%**, Filter 1: **Analog LP12 @ 1.8 kHz**  |\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | **Reverb:** Size **80%**, Decay **4.0 s**, Low Cut **250 Hz**|\n| **MODULATION**       | **LFO 1:** Free 0.1 Hz sweep on **Filter Cutoff**      |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §6.5"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-11","title":"13.2.11 — DnB Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.11 — DnB Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                          DNB LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Reese Low-Pass Cutoff (Dark -&gt; Bright)**                |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **Neuro Notch Frequency Sweep**                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Distortion Saturation Level**                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Foghorn Pitch Envelope Amount**                         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Reese Detune Width (Cents)**                            |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Sub-to-Mid Balance**                                    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **High-Frequency Chorus / Stereo Spread**                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master Delay / Reverb Throw**                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-2-12","title":"13.2.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 174 BPM Drop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.2.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 174 BPM Drop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Program a 174 BPM drum pattern (Kick on 1, Snare on Beat 2.5/4).","Insert a dedicated Sub Bass track (<code>Operator</code> Sine @ 55 Hz).","Insert a Reese mid-bass (<code>Surge XT</code> Dual Saws) and a Foghorn stab (<code>Operator</code>).","Alternate the Reese roll and Foghorn hit in a 4-bar rolling progression.","Export your final DnB drop stem as <code>SD_Lab_DnBDrop_174BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Drum-and-Bass-Production-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-3-3","code":"13.3","title":"House Music Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic architecture of House Music (120-128 BPM, four-on-the-floor kick, offbeat hi-hats, and subgenre variants across Deep, Tech, Bass, and Future House). - Synthesize all primary House instruments from scratch:","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-55","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic architecture of <strong>House Music</strong> (120-128 BPM, four-on-the-floor kick, offbeat hi-hats, and subgenre variants across Deep, Tech, Bass, and Future House).","Synthesize all primary House instruments from scratch:","<strong>Deep House FM Bass</strong> (<code>Operator</code> 1:2 ratio donk/pluck)","<strong>Tech House Rolling Bass</strong> (<code>Drift</code> / <code>Surge XT</code> 16th-note filter decay)","<strong>Bass House Growl-Pluck</strong> (<code>Vital</code> Formant Pluck)","<strong>Classic House Organ Stab</strong> (<code>Operator</code> Algorithm 11 Additive Organ)","<strong>Resampled Minor 9th Chord Stab</strong> (<code>Simpler</code> Pitch Slicing)","Synthesize the definitive <strong>909-Style House Kick</strong> and <strong>Offbeat Open Hi-Hat</strong>.","Calibrate 4-on-the-floor <strong>Sidechain Ducking Compression</strong>.","Construct a complete 124 BPM Deep / Tech House groove from scratch."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-1","title":"13.3.1 — House Music Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.1 — House Music Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"House music is anchored by a steady four-on-the-floor bass drum (120-128 BPM) with an open hi-hat on every offbeat (&amp; of every beat):"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                  HOUSE MUSIC RHYTHMIC TOPOLOGY                                    |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Beat:       1   .   &amp;   .   2   .   &amp;   .   3   .   &amp;   .   4   .   &amp;   .                         |\n| Kick:      [X]             [X]             [X]             [X]                                    |\n| Offbeat Hat:        [O]             [O]             [O]             [O]                           |\n| Bass Groove:    [B]     [B]     [B]     [B]     [B]     [B]     [B]     [B] (Syncopated / Rolling)|\n| Chord Stab: [S]                             [S]                                                   |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (House Sound Design)","<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.1"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-2","title":"13.3.2 — The Deep House FM Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.2 — The Deep House FM Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The signature sound of Deep House (pioneered by MK, Kerri Chandler, and modern deep house producers) is a pristine 2-operator 1:2 FM ratio:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: DEEP HOUSE FM BASS                                       |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 1** (or Alg 4)                             |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1** (Fund)  |\n| (Carrier)            | Level: **0.0 dB**, AEG: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **280 ms**|\n|                      | Sustain: **0.0**, Release: **35 ms**                   |\n| **OPERATOR B**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **2** (+1 Oct)|\n| (Modulator)          | Level: **-12.0 dB**, Envelope: Attack **0 ms**,        |\n|                      | Decay: **110 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**, Release: **35 ms**|\n| **FILTER**           | **Bypassed** (FM envelope provides all dynamic shaping)|\n| **VOICING**          | **Mono**, Glide: **Off**                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A warm, bouncy, rubbery FM bass punch that sits perfectly beneath deep house chords without crowding the mix."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe A)","<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 23"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-3","title":"13.3.3 — The Tech House Rolling Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.3 — The Tech House Rolling Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Tech House relies on a tight, driving 16th-note bassline rolling between four-on-the-floor kick strikes:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: TECH HOUSE ROLLING BASS                                  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Drift** (or Surge XT Classic)                |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Waveform: **Sawtooth**, Octave: **-1**, Level: **0 dB**|\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Waveform: **Square**, Octave: **-1**, Level: **-6 dB** |\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **Low-Pass LP12**, Cutoff: **140 Hz**, Res: **0.20**|\n| **FILTER ENVELOPE**  | Attack: **0 ms**, Decay: **95 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**   |\n|                      | Depth: **+45%** (Snappy 16th-note transient punch)     |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Saturator` (Drive +3 dB) -&gt; `Utility` (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz)|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A tight, dark, percussive bassline that locks relentlessly into the groove."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe B)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-4","title":"13.3.4 — Bass House / Future House Growl-Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.4 — Bass House / Future House Growl-Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: BASS HOUSE GROWL-PLUCK                                   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Warp: **Formant Scale** |\n| **ENVELOPE 2**       | Attack: **0 ms**, Decay: **180 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**  |\n|                      | - Route Env 2 to **Formant Scale (+60%)**              |\n|                      | - Route Env 2 to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+75%)**            |\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Dirty LP24**, Cutoff: **280 Hz**, Drive: **+5 dB**|\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Distortion:** Mode **Hard Clip**, Drive **+8 dB**  |\n|                      | 2. **Compressor:** Mode **Multiband**, Mix **70%**     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> An aggressive, metallic, vocal-edged bass stab engineered for high-energy Bass House drops."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 2 &amp; 7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-5","title":"13.3.5 — The Classic House Organ Stab","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.5 — The Classic House Organ Stab","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: CLASSIC 90s HOUSE ORGAN STAB                             |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 11** (Parallel Additive)                   |\n| **OSC A ($8'$)**     | Coarse: **1**, Level: **0.0 dB**, Decay: **350 ms**, Sust: **0.0**|\n| **OSC B ($4'$)**     | Coarse: **2**, Level: **-3.0 dB**, Decay: **280 ms**   |\n| **OSC C ($2\\tfrac{2}{3}'$)**| Coarse: **3**, Level: **-8.0 dB**, Decay: **200 ms**|\n| **OSC D ($2'$)**     | Coarse: **4**, Level: **-6.0 dB**, Decay: **180 ms**   |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Reverb` (Decay: 1.4 s, Low Cut: 300 Hz, Mix: 20%)     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> The quintessential Robin S / Nightcrawlers 1990s house organ stab."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §8 &amp; §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-6","title":"13.3.6 — Resampled Minor 9th / 11th Chord Stabs","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.6 — Resampled Minor 9th / 11th Chord Stabs","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The sonic hallmark of classic Detroit and Chicago house is the <strong>Sampled Chord Stab</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">1. RECORD A LUSH MINOR 9th CHORD ON A SYNTH (Notes: C3, Eb3, G3, Bb3, D4).\n2. RENDER THE CHORD TO A 1-SECOND AUDIO SAMPLE.\n3. LOAD THE AUDIO INTO ABLETON SIMPLER (Classic Mode, Complex Pro Warp).\n4. PLAY MELODIES WITH SINGLE KEYS ON THE KEYBOARD.</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Because every note on the keyboard plays the <em>exact same parallel chord interval</em>, the progression acquires the authentic, hypnotizing harmonic sound of vintage vinyl sampling."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe E)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-7","title":"13.3.7 — The 909-Style Synthetic House Kick","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.7 — The 909-Style Synthetic House Kick","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: 909 SYNTHETIC HOUSE KICK                                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 4**                                        |\n| **OSC A (Body)**     | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **0.5** (45 Hz)|\n|                      | AEG: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **420 ms**, Sustain **0.0**|\n| **OSC B (Click)**    | Mode: **Fixed (1.2 kHz)**, Level: **-14 dB**, Decay: **15 ms**|\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Amount: **+24 st**, Pitch Decay: **30 ms**              |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A tight, round, punchy 45 Hz house kick with a crisp 1.2 kHz beater click."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-8","title":"13.3.8 — Synthetic House Offbeat Open Hi-Hat","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.8 — Synthetic House Offbeat Open Hi-Hat","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: 909 OFFBEAT OPEN HI-HAT                                  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 11**                                       |\n| **OSC A**            | Mode: **Fixed (9.5 kHz)**, Wave: **Noise White**       |\n|                      | AEG: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **160 ms**, Sustain **0.0**|\n|                      | Release: **40 ms**                                     |\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **High-Pass HP24**, Cutoff: **7.8 kHz**          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A crisp, sizzling open hi-hat that lifts the offbeat energy of any house groove."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-9","title":"13.3.9 — 4-on-the-Floor Sidechain Ducking","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.9 — 4-on-the-Floor Sidechain Ducking","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ KICK TRACK (Quarter Notes) ] ===(Sidechain Audio)===&gt; [ COMPRESSOR (On Bass &amp; Chords) ]\n                                                                      |\n                                                                      v\n                                                  [ Ducks Volume 6 dB on Beats 1, 2, 3, 4 ]\n                                                  [ Releases Gain on the Offbeat '&amp;' ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Calibration:</strong> Attack = 0.5 ms, Release = 90 ms - 120 ms (timed so the bass returns to full volume exactly when the offbeat hi-hat strikes)."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §13"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-10","title":"13.3.10 — Assembling the House Groove Grid","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.10 — Assembling the House Groove Grid","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">TRACK 1: 909 Kick          (Quarter Notes: 1, 2, 3, 4)\nTRACK 2: Offbeat Open Hat  (Offbeats: 1&amp;, 2&amp;, 3&amp;, 4&amp;)\nTRACK 3: Deep FM Bass      (Syncopated 16th-note bounce)\nTRACK 4: Minor 9th Stab    (Hits on Beat 1 and the 3&amp;)\nTRACK 5: Sidechain Glue    (Compressor sidechained to Track 1)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-11","title":"13.3.11 — House Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.11 — House Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                         HOUSE LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                             |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Bass Filter Cutoff / Brightness**                       |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **Bass Decay Length (Pluck -&gt; Sustained)**                |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Chord Stab Reverb Mix**                                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Chord Filter Cutoff Sweep**                             |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Hat Decay Length (Tight Closed -&gt; Sizzling Open)**      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Sidechain Ducking Depth**                               |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Saturator Drive on Bass**                               |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master High-Pass Filter (Drop Sweep)**                  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-3-12","title":"13.3.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 124 BPM House Groove","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.3.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 124 BPM House Groove","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Set project tempo to 124 BPM.","Synthesize a 909-style kick in <code>Operator</code> and program 4-on-the-floor quarter notes.","Synthesize an offbeat open hi-hat in <code>Operator</code> on every &amp; beat.","Synthesize a Deep FM bass in <code>Operator</code> (1:2 ratio) and program a bouncy 2-bar bassline.","Create a minor 9th chord stab in <code>Simpler</code> and place hits on Beat 1 and Beat 3.5.","Export your complete groove stem as <code>SD_Lab_HouseGroove_124BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-4-4","code":"13.4","title":"Techno Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic architecture of Techno (130-145 BPM, hypnotic repetition, industrial rumble kicks, minimalist precision). - Synthesize all primary Techno sound design elements from scratch:","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-56","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic architecture of <strong>Techno</strong> (130-145 BPM, hypnotic repetition, industrial rumble kicks, minimalist precision).","Synthesize all primary Techno sound design elements from scratch:","<strong>The Sub-Rumble Kick</strong> (Reverberant low-passed kick rumble)","<strong>Industrial Dark Stab</strong> (<code>Surge XT</code> K35 Filter + Saturated Saw)","<strong>Resonant Acid 303 Bassline</strong> (<code>Drift</code> Saturated Ladder)","<strong>Metallic Inharmonic Percussion</strong> (<code>Operator</code> Inharmonic FM)","<strong>Hypnotic Sequenced Modular Lead</strong> (<code>Surge XT</code> 16-Step StepSeq)","Assemble an 8-knob Techno Performance Template for the Launchkey MK4.","Construct a complete 135 BPM Peak-Time Techno groove from scratch."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-1","title":"13.4.1 — Techno Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.1 — Techno Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Modern Peak-Time and Raw/Hypnotic Techno is driven by relentless industrial energy (130-145 BPM), heavy low-end acoustic rumble, and evolving micro-timbral automation:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                     TECHNO FREQUENCY TOPOLOGY                                     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| FREQUENCY BAND    | ACOUSTIC ROLE               | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | PROCESSING PROTOCOL     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$30 - 120\\text{ Hz}$**| **Rumble Sub-Bass Bed**     | Resampled Kick Reverb | **Low-Pass @ 130 Hz**,  |\n|                   | (Endless sub rolling wave)  | (Processed kick tail) | Heavy Sidechain to Kick |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$200 - 800\\text{ Hz}$**| **Saturated Acid / Stabs**  | `Drift` / `Surge XT`  | Sallen-Key K35 Grit,    |\n|                   | (Dark, hypnotic repetitions)| (Saw / Square Squelch)| Pre-filter Overdrive    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$&gt;2\\text{ kHz}$**| **Industrial FM Clank**     | `Operator` Fixed FM   | Short Plate Reverb,     |\n|                   | (Metallic hats &amp; shakers)   | (Inharmonic ratios)   | Redux bit reduction     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Techno Sound Design)","<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-2","title":"13.4.2 — The Techno Rumble Kick","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.2 — The Techno Rumble Kick","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The defining low-end foundation of modern Berlin and Peak-Time techno is the <strong>Reverberant Sub-Rumble Kick</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ DRY PUNCHY 909 KICK ] ===(Direct Out)===========================================&gt; [ KICK TRANSIENT ]\n         |                                                                                  +\n         +===(Send to Parallel Rumble Chain)===&gt; [ REVERB (Decay: 2.5s, 100% Wet) ]         |\n                                             ===&gt; [ SATURATOR (Drive: +8 dB, Hard Clip) ]   |\n                                             ===&gt; [ LOW-PASS FILTER (LP24 @ 120 Hz) ]       |\n                                             ===&gt; [ COMPRESSOR (Sidechained to Dry Kick) ]  |\n                                             ===&gt; [ UTILITY (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz) ] =======&gt; [ SUB RUMBLE ]</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Step-by-Step Construction:","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Program a dry 4-on-the-floor kick on Track 1.","Create an Audio Effect Rack with two chains: <strong><code>Dry Kick</code></strong> and <strong><code>Rumble Chain</code></strong>.","On the <code>Rumble Chain</code>:","Insert <code>Reverb</code> (100% Wet, Size 80%, Decay 2.0 s).","Insert <code>Saturator</code> (Drive +9 dB, Curve: Hard Clip).","Insert <code>Auto Filter</code> (Low-Pass 24 dB, Cutoff 120 Hz).","Insert <code>Compressor</code> (Sidechain enabled, listening to Dry Kick, Fast Attack, Release 80 ms).","Insert <code>Utility</code> (Mono enabled)."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> The reverb tail of the kick is heavily distorted, low-passed into a sub wave, and ducked out of the way every time the dry kick strikes, creating an endless, rolling low-frequency freight train."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe C)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-3","title":"13.4.3 — Industrial Dark Stab","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.3 — Industrial Dark Stab","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: INDUSTRIAL TECHNO DARK STAB                              |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Surge XT**                                           |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Algorithm: **Classic**, Shape: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **0**|\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Algorithm: **Classic**, Shape: **Sawtooth**, Detune: **+14c**|\n| **FILTER 1**         | Model: **Vintage K35 (LP18)**, Cutoff: **380 Hz**, Res: **0.50**|\n| **WAVESHAPER**       | Model: **Hard Clip**, Drive: **+8.5 dB**               |\n| **ENVELOPES**        | - **AEG:** Attack **0 ms**, Decay **220 ms**, Sustain **0.0**|\n|                      | - **FEG:** Attack **0 ms**, Decay **120 ms**, Sustain **0.0**|\n|                      |   Route FEG to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+50%)**              |\n| **EFFECTS BUS**      | **Airwindows Galactic Reverb**, Size: **70%**, Mix: **25%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A dark, reverberant, industrial warehouse stab with aggressive MS-20 resonant grit."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Surge XT User Manual</em>, Section 2 &amp; 4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-4","title":"13.4.4 — Resonant Acid 303 Bassline","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.4 — Resonant Acid 303 Bassline","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: SQUELCHY 303 ACID BASS                                   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Drift**                                      |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Waveform: **Sawtooth**, Octave: **-1**                 |\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **Low-Pass LP24 (Saturated)**, Cutoff: **240 Hz**|\n|                      | Resonance: **0.82** (Near Self-Oscillation Squelch)    |\n| **FILTER ENVELOPE**  | Attack: **0 ms**, Decay: **140 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**   |\n|                      | Envelope Amount: **+75%**                              |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Overdrive` (Drive +5 dB) -&gt; `Delay` (1/16th Dotted)   |\n| **VOICING**          | Mode: **Mono Legato**, Glide Time: **60 ms**           |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A screaming, squelchy Roland TB-303 acid line that accentuates and slides across 16th-note patterns."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe D)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-5","title":"13.4.5 — FM Metallic Percussion","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.5 — FM Metallic Percussion","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: TECHNO METALLIC INHARMONIC PERCUSSION                   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 1**                                        |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **1**         |\n|                      | AEG Decay: **65 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**                 |\n| **OPERATOR B**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Square D**, Coarse: **3**, Fine: **0.414**|\n|                      | Level: **-6.0 dB**, AEG Decay: **35 ms**               |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Redux` (Quantize: 10 bit) -&gt; `Filter Delay` (1/16th)  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A biting, clangorous industrial anvil strike that cuts through driving techno basslines."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 23"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-6","title":"13.4.6 — Hypnotic 16-Step Sequenced Lead","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.6 — Hypnotic 16-Step Sequenced Lead","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: HYPNOTIC SEQUENCED MODULAR LEAD                          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Surge XT**                                           |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Algorithm: **Twist**, Model: **Modal Resonator**       |\n| **MODULATION**       | **Voice LFO 1:** Shape: **StepSeq**, Rate: **1/16th Sync**|\n|                      | - Program 16-step rhythmic pattern                     |\n|                      | - Route StepSeq LFO 1 to **Twist Timbre (+70%)**       |\n|                      | - Route StepSeq LFO 1 to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+50%)**    |\n| **EFFECTS BUS**      | **Stereo Ping-Pong Delay**, Sync: **1/8thD**, Mix: **20%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A mesmerizing, evolving modular sequence that loops continuously across 1-bar patterns."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Surge XT User Manual</em>, Section 2.9 &amp; 5.4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-7","title":"13.4.7 — White Noise Tension Sweeps","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.7 — White Noise Tension Sweeps","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: 8-BAR TECHNO NOISE RISER                                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator** (or Drift)                        |\n| **OSCILLATOR**       | Waveform: **Noise White**                              |\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **Band-Pass BP24**, Cutoff: **200 Hz**, Res: **0.60**|\n| **AUTOMATION**       | Automate Cutoff from **200 Hz -&gt; 8 kHz over 8 Bars**   |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Phaser-Flanger` (8 Poles) -&gt; `Reverb` (Decay: 6.0 s)  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-8","title":"13.4.8 — Distortion and Saturation Chains for Techno","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.8 — Distortion and Saturation Chains for Techno","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ TECHNO SYNTH VOICE ] ===&gt; [ SATURATOR (Analog Clip: +4 dB) ]\n                       ===&gt; [ REDUX (Rate Downsample: 32 kHz, Jitter 20%) ]\n                       ===&gt; [ OVERDRIVE (Freq: 1.8 kHz, Drive +5 dB) ]\n                       ===&gt; [ UTILITY (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz) ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-9","title":"13.4.9 — Techno Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.9 — Techno Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                         TECHNO LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                            |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Rumble Sub-Bass Level / Cutoff**                        |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **Acid 303 Resonance ($Q$) Squelch**                      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Acid Cutoff Envelope Amount**                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Dark Stab Reverb Size &amp; Decay**                         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Overdrive Saturation Distortion**                       |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Redux Bitcrush Amount**                                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Delay Feedback Swell**                                  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master High-Pass Filter (Drop Builder)**                |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-4-10","title":"13.4.10 — Lab: Building a Complete 135 BPM Techno Groove","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.4.10 — Lab: Building a Complete 135 BPM Techno Groove","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Set project tempo to 135 BPM.","Build a 4-on-the-floor 909 kick and parallel Rumble Sub chain.","Synthesize a squelchy Acid 303 bassline in <code>Drift</code> and program a continuous 16th-note rolling sequence.","Synthesize an industrial dark stab in <code>Surge XT</code> hitting on the offbeats of Beats 2 and 4.","Synthesize inharmonic metallic hats in <code>Operator</code> on 16th-note upbeats.","Export your finished Peak-Time Techno groove stem as <code>SD_Lab_TechnoGroove_135BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-5-5","code":"13.5","title":"UK Garage Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic and rhythmic architecture of UK Garage (UKG) (130-138 BPM, 2-step syncopation, 55-71% swing shuffle, sub-bass dominance, and lineage connecting House, Jungle, 2-Step, and Dubstep). - Synthesize all primary UK Garage in","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-57","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic and rhythmic architecture of <strong>UK Garage (UKG)</strong> (130-138 BPM, 2-step syncopation, 55-71% swing shuffle, sub-bass dominance, and lineage connecting House, Jungle, 2-Step, and Dubstep).","Synthesize all primary UK Garage instruments from scratch:","<strong>The UKG Sub Bass</strong> (Pure mono sine / saturated triangle with legato glide)","<strong>The Bouncy UKG Reese / Mid-Bass Pluck</strong> (Detuned saws with snappy LPF decay)","<strong>The Classic UKG Organ Stab</strong> (<code>Operator</code> FM Organ / Korg M1 heritage)","<strong>Minor 7th / 9th Sampled Chord Stabs</strong> (<code>Simpler</code> Slicing)","<strong>UKG Pitched Vocal Chop Melodies</strong> (<code>Simpler</code> Complex Pro Formant Slicing)","<strong>Bright Sine / Triangle Melodic Leads</strong>","Synthesize <strong>2-Step Syncopated Drums</strong> (Tight Kick, Snappy Rimshot/Snare, Shuffled Ghost Hats).","Apply the <strong>Live 12 Swing Engine (55% - 71%)</strong> to sound design envelopes.","Construct a complete 134 BPM 2-Step UK Garage track from scratch."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-1","title":"13.5.1 — UK Garage Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.1 — UK Garage Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"UK Garage emerged in London in the mid-1990s, evolving from 4-on-the-floor American house by stripping out the kicks on beats 2 and 4, injecting syncopated jungle-derived swing (55-71%), and prioritizing massive, rolling sub-bass weight:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                     UKG RHYTHMIC TOPOLOGY (2-STEP)                                |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Metric Beat:  1   .   &amp;   .   2   .   &amp;   .   3   .   &amp;   .   4   .   &amp;   .                       |\n| 2-Step Kick: [X]                         [X]                 (No Kick on Beat 2 or 4!)            |\n| Snare / Rim:                 [S]                             [S]                                  |\n| Shuffled Hat:    [h] [H]   [h]   [h] [H]   [h]   [h] [H]   [h]   [h] [H]   [h] (58% Swing Grid)   |\n| Bouncy Reese:    [B]     [B]         [B]             [B]   [B]                                    |\n| Organ Stab:  [O]                 [O]                                                              |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| Parameter        | Standard Specification| Musical Sound Design Function                      |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Tempo**        | **$130 - 138\\text{ BPM}$**| Faster than House ($124$), slower than DnB ($174$).|\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Groove Swing** | **$55\\% - 71\\%$**     | Pushes 16th-note upbeats late for infectious bounce.|\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Bass Lineage** | Reggae / Jungle Sub   | Deep monophonic sine sub anchored beneath bouncy mid.|\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §1 &amp; §2","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-2","title":"13.5.2 — The UKG Sub Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.2 — The UKG Sub Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"UKG sub-bass must provide heavy low-frequency pressure (35-80 Hz) that rolls smoothly between syncopated kick strikes:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: UKG PURE SUB BASS                                        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator** (or Drift)                        |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 11**                                       |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **0.5** (Sub) |\n|                      | Level: **0.0 dB**, AEG: Attack **2 ms**, Decay **800 ms**|\n|                      | Sustain: **0.85**, Release: **45 ms**                  |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Saturator` (Soft Sine, Drive: +2 dB) -&gt; `Utility` (Mono)|\n| **VOICING**          | Mode: **Mono Legato**, Glide Time: **55 ms**           |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A warm, deep, rounded sub-bass that glides expressively across rolling 2-step basslines."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-3","title":"13.5.3 — The Bouncy UKG Reese / Mid-Bass Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.3 — The Bouncy UKG Reese / Mid-Bass Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Unlike the dark, sustained neurofunk Reese of DnB, the <strong>UKG Reese Pluck</strong> is bright, snappy, and heavily envelope-decayed to bounce in time with the swing grid:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: BOUNCY UKG REESE PLUCK                                   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Surge XT** (or Vital)                                |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Algorithm: **Classic**, Shape: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **-1**|\n|                      | Detune: **-16 cents**                                  |\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Algorithm: **Classic**, Shape: **Sawtooth**, Oct: **-1**|\n|                      | Detune: **+16 cents** (Wide 32-cent phase beating)     |\n| **FILTER 1**         | Model: **Ladder 24 dB**, Cutoff: **180 Hz**, Res: **0.25**|\n| **FILTER ENVELOPE**  | Attack: **0 ms**, **Decay: 160 ms**, Sustain: **0.0**  |\n|                      | Route FEG to **Filter 1 Cutoff (+65%)**                |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Saturator` (Drive +4 dB) -&gt; `EQ Eight` (HP @ 110 Hz)  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A rubbery, vocal, detuned Reese pluck that opens on note attack and decays rapidly, leaving space for the sub-bass to dominate the low end."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §2 &amp; §3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-4","title":"13.5.4 — The Classic UKG Organ Stab (Korg M1 Heritage)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.4 — The Classic UKG Organ Stab (Korg M1 Heritage)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The definitive musical element of 1990s 2-step (Todd Edwards, MJ Cole, Grant Nelson) is the <strong>FM Organ Stab</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: CLASSIC UKG 2-STEP ORGAN STAB                            |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 11** (Additive Drawbars)                   |\n| **OSC A ($16'$)**    | Coarse: **0.5**, Level: **0.0 dB**, Decay: **260 ms**  |\n| **OSC B ($8'$)**     | Coarse: **1**, Level: **-2.0 dB**, Decay: **240 ms**   |\n| **OSC C ($5\\tfrac{1}{3}'$)**| Coarse: **1.5**, Level: **-4.0 dB**, Decay: **200 ms**|\n| **OSC D ($4'$)**     | Coarse: **2**, Level: **-6.0 dB**, Decay: **180 ms**   |\n| **ENVELOPES**        | All Sustain levels at **0.0** (Strict percussive stab) |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Reverb` (Decay: 1.2 s, Low Cut: 250 Hz, Mix: 22%)     |\n| **VOICING**          | **Polyphony: 6 Voices**                                |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A punchy, hollow, percussive organ chord stab that punches on syncopated upbeats."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §3","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-5","title":"13.5.5 — UKG Minor 7th and Minor 9th Chord Stabs","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.5 — UKG Minor 7th and Minor 9th Chord Stabs","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">1. RECORD A JAZZ MINOR 9th CHORD (Notes: D3, F3, A3, C4, E4) USING ELECTRIC (RHODES MODEL).\n2. RENDER THE CHORD TO AUDIO AND LOAD INTO SIMPLER (Classic Mode).\n3. APPLY FILTER: Low-Pass LP12 @ 2.4 kHz with snappy Filter Decay (200 ms).\n4. INSERT REVERB (Plate Mode, Mix 25%) AND GLUE COMPRESSOR.</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Triggering this chord stab across the MIDI keyboard creates authentic 1998-era speed garage and 2-step chord progressions."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-6","title":"13.5.6 — Bright Sine / Triangle Melodic Leads","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.6 — Bright Sine / Triangle Melodic Leads","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: UKG 2-STEP SINE LEAD                                     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital** (or Operator)                                |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Waveform: **Triangle**, Octave: **0**                  |\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Waveform: **Sine**, Octave: **+1**, Level: **-8 dB**   |\n| **LFO 1 (Vibrato)**  | Rate: **5.5 Hz**, Depth: **15 cents** (Delayed onset)  |\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Delay:** Ping-Pong (1/8th Dotted, Mix: 25%)       |\n|                      | 2. **Reverb:** Size **70%**, Decay **3.0 s**, Mix **30%**|\n| **VOICING**          | **Mono Legato**, Glide Time: **40 ms**                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A delicate, bright, floating melodic lead that weaves between vocal chops and heavy sub-bass."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §5"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-7","title":"13.5.7 — Pitched Vocal Chops: Formant Warping","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.7 — Pitched Vocal Chops: Formant Warping","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The defining melodic hook of UK Garage is the <strong>Pitched-Up Female Vocal Chop</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ DRY R&amp;B VOCAL SAMPLE ] ===&gt; [ DRAG INTO SIMPLER (Slicing Mode) ]\n                                            |\n                                            +---&gt; Slicing: Transient (Sensitivity: 60%)\n                                            +---&gt; Warp: ON (Mode: COMPLEX PRO)\n                                            +---&gt; Formant Slider: 100 (Preserves Throat Tone)\n                                            +---&gt; Transpose: +5 or +7 Semitones</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Slicing vocal syllables (\"Baby\", \"Love\", \"Yeah\") and playing them as rhythmic melodic hooks over a swung 2-step beat creates the emotional foundation of UK Garage."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-8","title":"13.5.8 — UKG Drum Synthesis: 2-Step Kick and Snare","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.8 — UKG Drum Synthesis: 2-Step Kick and Snare","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| SYNTHETIC 2-STEP KICK:                                                        |\n| - Engine: `Operator` (Single Sine, Pitch Env: +24 st -&gt; 55 Hz in 28 ms)       |\n| - Fast, tight, short decay (240 ms) so it doesn't collide with syncopated sub.|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| SYNTHETIC UKG RIMSHOT / SNARE:                                                |\n| - Engine: `Collision` (Wood Beam Mallet) + `Operator` (Noise Burst)           |\n| - Crisp, high-frequency wooden crack hitting strictly on Beats 2 and 4.       |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §6 &amp; §8"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-9","title":"13.5.9 — The UKG Swing Engine: Live 12 Groove Pool","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.9 — The UKG Swing Engine: Live 12 Groove Pool","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To lock your sound design envelopes to authentic UKG shuffle:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ ABLETON LIVE 12 GROOVE POOL ] ===&gt; Select: \"Swing 16ths - 58%\" (or 64%)\n                                                   |\n                                                   v\n                                 [ APPLY TO MIDI CLIPS &amp; ENVELOPES ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["When swing is engaged, the 2nd, 4th, 6th, and 8th 16th-notes are delayed in time, causing the decay curves of your Reese plucks and hi-hats to align with human rhythmic bounce."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §6","<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 14 (Using Grooves)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-10","title":"13.5.10 — Sub-Genre Adaptations","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.10 — Sub-Genre Adaptations","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| UKG Sub-Genre      | Sound Design Adaptation                                          |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Speed Garage**   | Four-on-the-floor kick + Heavy time-stretched 4x4 Reese bass.   |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **2-Step**         | Syncopated kick (Beat 1 and Beat 3.5) + Hollow FM organ stabs.   |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Future Garage**  | Burial-style ambient vinyl crackle, pitch-down vocals, lush pads.|\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Bassline / 4x4** | Screaming FM donks, distorted square leads, fast 4x4 drive.      |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-11","title":"13.5.11 — UKG Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.11 — UKG Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                          UKG LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Sub Bass Glide Time**                                   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **Reese Pluck Filter Decay (Short Pluck -&gt; Open Growl)**  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Organ Stab Reverb Mix**                                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Organ Brightness (Osc D Level)**                        |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Vocal Chop Filter Cutoff**                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Hi-Hat Decay Length (Tight Closed -&gt; Swung Open)**      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Saturator Drive on Reese**                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master High-Pass Filter (Drop Sweep)**                  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-5-12","title":"13.5.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 134 BPM 2-Step UKG Track","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.5.12 — Lab: Building a Complete 134 BPM 2-Step UKG Track","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Set project tempo to 134 BPM and load <strong><code>Swing 16ths 60%</code></strong> in the Groove Pool.","Program a syncopated 2-step drum beat (Kick on Beat 1 and Beat 3.5, Snare on Beats 2 and 4).","Synthesize a gliding sub-bass in <code>Operator</code> (55 ms glide).","Synthesize an FM organ stab in <code>Operator</code> and program a syncopated chord progression.","Create a pitched vocal chop instrument in <code>Simpler</code> (+5 semitones) and program a melodic call-and-response hook.","Export your complete 2-Step UK Garage track stem as <code>SD_Lab_UKGarage_134BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>UK Garage Research Specialist Report</em>, §8"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-6-6","code":"13.6","title":"Trap & 808 Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic architecture of Trap & Hip-Hop Sound Design (130-160 BPM / 65-80 BPM half-time, sub dominance from 30-65 Hz, gliding 808 slides, rapid multi-rate hi-hat rolls, and brass stabs). - Synthesize all primary Trap instrument","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-58","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic architecture of <strong>Trap &amp; Hip-Hop Sound Design</strong> (130-160 BPM / 65-80 BPM half-time, sub dominance from 30-65 Hz, gliding 808 slides, rapid multi-rate hi-hat rolls, and brass stabs).","Synthesize all primary Trap instruments completely from scratch:","<strong>The Classic 808 Sub Bass</strong> (<code>Operator</code> Pure Sine + Pitch Envelope + Soft Saturation)","<strong>The Gliding Legato 808</strong> (Multi-octave pitch slides)","<strong>The Distorted Mobile-Ready 808</strong> (<code>Saturator</code> + <code>Erosion</code> + <code>Dynamic Tube</code>)","<strong>The Short Punchy 808</strong> (Kick-808 hybrid)","<strong>Synthetic Trap Brass Lead</strong> (<code>Drift</code> Unison Saws + Pitch Scoop)","<strong>Synthetic Hi-Hats &amp; Multi-Rate Rolls</strong> (<code>Operator</code> Noise + High-Pass)","<strong>Synthetic Trap Snare / Clap Layer</strong>","Construct a complete 140 BPM (70 BPM half-time) Trap beat from scratch."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-1","title":"13.6.1 — Trap Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.1 — Trap Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Trap music is structured around an ultra-spacious half-time groove (130-160 BPM master clock, felt as 65-80 BPM half-time). The entire low-end frequency spectrum is surrendered to a sustained, pitch-sliding <strong>808 Sub-Bass</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                      TRAP FREQUENCY TOPOLOGY                                      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| FREQUENCY BAND    | ACOUSTIC ROLE               | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | PROCESSING PROTOCOL     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$30 - 65\\text{ Hz}$**| **808 Sub-Bass Fundamental**| `Operator` / `Drift`  | **Pure Sine / Triangle**|\n|                   | (Massive sustained weight)  | (Single pure carrier) | Mono Legato Glide       |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$700\\text{ Hz}-3\\text{ kHz}$**| **808 Upper Harmonic Buzz** | `Erosion` / `Saturator`| Audible on phone /     |\n|                   | (Allows 808 to be heard)    | (Sine Mode / Soft Clip)| laptop speakers         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$&gt;8\\text{ kHz}$**| **Rolling Hi-Hat Sizzle**   | `Operator` White Noise| High-pass @ 8.5 kHz,    |\n|                   | (1/16th, 1/32nd, triplets)  | (Snappy short decay)  | Pitch-shifted rolls     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Trap / 808 Sound Design)","<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.5"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-2","title":"13.6.2 — The 808 Sub Bass from Scratch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.2 — The 808 Sub Bass from Scratch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: CLASSIC CLEAN 808 SUB BASS                              |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **ALGORITHM**        | **Algorithm 11** (Single Carrier)                      |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Coarse: **0.5** (Sub) |\n|                      | Level: **0.0 dB**, Phase: **0 degrees (Retrigger ON)** |\n|                      | AEG: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **2.5 s**, Sustain **0.80**,|\n|                      | Release: **50 ms**                                     |\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Amount: **+24 semitones**, Pitch Decay: **22 ms**      |\n|                      | (Creates the punchy attack transient thud)             |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Saturator` (Soft Sine, Drive: +3 dB) -&gt; `Utility` (Mono)|\n| **VOICING**          | Mode: **Mono**, Glide: **Off**                         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A pristine, deep, chest-rattling 808 sub-bass with a punchy 22 ms attack drop that sustains smoothly for over 2 seconds."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 &amp; §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-3","title":"13.6.3 — The Gliding Legato 808","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.3 — The Gliding Legato 808","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To execute multi-octave 808 slides (e.g., sliding from C_1 up to G_2 and dropping to F_1):"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ MIDI NOTE C1 HELD ] ===(Overlapping Note G2 Struck)===&gt; [ PITCH GLIDES SMOOTHLY OVER 110 ms ]</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| Voicing Control  | Calibration           | Function                                           |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Polyphony**    | **Mono (1 Voice)**    | Prevents overlapping 808 notes from phase canceling.|\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Legato Mode**  | **ON**                | Pitch glide activates ONLY when MIDI notes overlap!|\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Glide Time**   | **$90\\text{ ms} - 140\\text{ ms}$**| Calibrates musical slide speed between octaves.    |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 23 (Operator Voicing / Glide)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-4","title":"13.6.4 — The Distorted Mobile-Ready 808","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.4 — The Distorted Mobile-Ready 808","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To ensure an 808 remains clearly audible on mobile phone and laptop speakers without destroying its clean sub-bass foundation:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ CLEAN 808 SINE ] ===&gt; [ SATURATOR (Drive +5 dB, Analog Clip) ]\n                   ===&gt; [ EROSION (Mode: Sine, Freq: 3.5 kHz, Amount: 35) ]\n                   ===&gt; [ DYNAMIC TUBE (Bias: 50%, Drive: +3 dB) ]\n                   ===&gt; [ UTILITY (Bass Mono @ 120 Hz) ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Saturator:</strong> Adds 2nd and 3rd harmonics (100-300 Hz).","<strong>Erosion (Sine Mode):</strong> Modulates a dedicated 3.5 kHz frequency into the 808, providing clear, cutting top-end presence that translates on tiny phone speakers.","<strong>Dynamic Tube:</strong> Adds warm asymmetrical even harmonics.","<strong>Utility (Bass Mono):</strong> Keeps the low sub fundamental (&lt;120 Hz) strictly centered in mono."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §10 &amp; §13"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-5","title":"13.6.5 — The Short Punchy 808 (Kick Replacement)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.5 — The Short Punchy 808 (Kick Replacement)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"In modern minimalist trap, producers often eliminate the separate kick drum entirely and use a single short, punchy 808 to serve as both the kick and the bass:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: SHORT PUNCHY KICK-808                                    |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Wave: **Sine**, Level: **0.0 dB**, AEG Decay: **450 ms**|\n|                      | Sustain: **0.0** (Strict percussive drop)              |\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Amount: **+36 semitones**, Pitch Decay: **18 ms**      |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Drum Buss` (Drive: +4 dB, Transients: +0.40)          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.6"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-6","title":"13.6.6 — Synthetic Trap Brass Lead","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.6 — Synthetic Trap Brass Lead","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: AGGRESSIVE TRAP BRASS STAB                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Drift** (or Vital)                           |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Waveform: **Sawtooth**, Octave: **0**                  |\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Waveform: **Sawtooth**, Octave: **0**, Detune: **+12 cents**|\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **Low-Pass LP24**, Cutoff: **850 Hz**, Res: **0.30**|\n| **FILTER ENVELOPE**  | Attack: **15 ms** (Brass swell), Decay: **380 ms**, Sust: **0.20**|\n|                      | Depth: **+65%**                                        |\n| **PITCH ENVELOPE**   | Amount: **+12 st**, Pitch Decay: **35 ms** (Scoop-in)  |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Overdrive` (Drive +6 dB) -&gt; `Reverb` (Decay: 2.2 s)   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> An authoritative, menacing brass horn stab with a dynamic pitch scoop and biting analog saturation."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-7","title":"13.6.7 — Synthetic Trap Hi-Hats & Multi-Rate Rolls","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.7 — Synthetic Trap Hi-Hats & Multi-Rate Rolls","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: SYNTHETIC TRAP CLOSED HI-HAT                             |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator**                                   |\n| **OPERATOR A**       | Mode: **Fixed (10 kHz)**, Wave: **Noise White**        |\n|                      | AEG: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **45 ms**, Sustain **0.0** |\n| **FILTER**           | Mode: **High-Pass HP24**, Cutoff: **8.5 kHz**          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Multi-Rate Rolls:</strong> In the Live 12 MIDI Editor, change grid resolution between <strong>1/16th</strong>, <strong>1/24th (1/16T)</strong>, and <strong>1/32nd notes</strong>, automating pitch transposition downward across the roll."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 10 &amp; 23"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-8","title":"13.6.8 — Synthetic Trap Snare / Clap Layer","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.8 — Synthetic Trap Snare / Clap Layer","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: TRAP SNARE / CLAP HYBRID                                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Ableton Operator** (Algorithm 4)                     |\n| **OSC A (Body)**     | Mode: **Ratio**, Wave: **Sine**, Pitch: 180 Hz, Decay: 140 ms|\n| **OSC C (Clap Snap)**| Mode: **Fixed (6 kHz)**, Wave: **Noise White**         |\n|                      | Envelope: 3 rapid 5ms attack blips -&gt; 160 ms tail      |\n| **DOWNSTREAM FX**    | `Dynamic Tube` (Drive +5 dB) -&gt; `Glue Compressor`      |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-9","title":"13.6.9 — Trap Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.9 — Trap Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                          TRAP LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                             |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **808 Decay Length (Short Thud -&gt; Long Sustained Sub)**   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **808 Glide Time (Slide Speed)**                          |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **808 Distortion / Erosion Sizzle**                       |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **Brass Filter Cutoff (Dark -&gt; Blaring)**                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Brass Pitch Scoop Amount**                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Hi-Hat Decay Length**                                   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Snare Crack Snap**                                      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master Reverb Space**                                   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-6-10","title":"13.6.10 — Lab: Building a Complete 140 BPM Trap Beat","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.6.10 — Lab: Building a Complete 140 BPM Trap Beat","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Set project tempo to 140 BPM (Half-time grid).","Synthesize an 808 Sub Bass in <code>Operator</code> with Mono Legato (110 ms glide) and program a sliding bassline with octave jumps.","Synthesize synthetic trap hi-hats in <code>Operator</code> and program a pattern combining straight 16ths with 32nd-note pitch-dropped rolls.","Place a synthetic snare/clap on Beat 3 of every bar.","Synthesize a brass stab in <code>Drift</code> hitting on Beat 1 and the upbeat of Beat 4.","Export your complete Trap beat stem as <code>SD_Lab_TrapBeat_140BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-13-7-7","code":"13.7","title":"Future Bass & Melodic EDM Sound-Design Lab","blurb":"- Master the acoustic architecture of Future Bass & Melodic EDM (140-160 BPM half-time, massive supersaw chord stacks, dynamic LFO pumping sidechains, expressive pitch-scoop onsets, and vocal chop leads). - Synthesize all primary Future Bas","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-59","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the acoustic architecture of <strong>Future Bass &amp; Melodic EDM</strong> (140-160 BPM half-time, massive supersaw chord stacks, dynamic LFO pumping sidechains, expressive pitch-scoop onsets, and vocal chop leads).","Synthesize all primary Future Bass instruments completely from scratch:","<strong>The 32-Voice Euphoric Supersaw Stack</strong> (<code>Vital</code> Multi-Oscillator Unison)","<strong>The Rhythmic Pumping Chord LFO</strong> (Automated volume &amp; filter pump)","<strong>The Pitch-Bend Scoop Onset Gesture</strong> (Dynamic transient scoop)","<strong>The Bright Melodic Chime Pluck</strong> (<code>Vital</code> Comb / Square Pluck)","<strong>Expressive Vocal Chop Lead</strong> (<code>Simpler</code> Complex Pro + Formant Slicing)","Construct extended <strong>Major 7th, Minor 9th, and Add9 Chord Voicings</strong>.","Assemble an 8-knob Future Bass Performance Template for the Launchkey MK4.","Construct a complete 150 BPM Future Bass drop from scratch.","Complete the <strong>Gate J Self-Assessment Checkpoint</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-1","title":"13.7.1 — Future Bass Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.1 — Future Bass Sonic Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Future Bass combines the half-time rhythmic punch of trap (140-160 BPM, felt as 70-80 BPM) with lush, emotional jazz harmonies, massive multi-voice supersaw chords, and dynamic rhythmic sidechain pumping:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                 FUTURE BASS FREQUENCY TOPOLOGY                                    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| FREQUENCY BAND    | ACOUSTIC ROLE               | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | PROCESSING BEHAVIOR     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$30 - 70\\text{ Hz}$**| **Clean 808 Sub Foundation**| `Operator` / `Drift`  | **Pure Mono Sine**,     |\n|                   | (Deep, solid low-end floor) | (Single clean sine)   | Zero Stereo FX          |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$150\\text{ Hz}-6\\text{ kHz}$**| **Massive Supersaw Chords** | `Vital` / `Surge XT`  | 32-Voice Unison,        |\n|                   | (Emotional harmonic weight) | (Stacked detuned saws)| Multiband Compression   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **$&gt;3\\text{ kHz}$**| **Melodic Plucks &amp; Vocals** | `Simpler` / `Vital`   | Ping-Pong Delay,        |\n|                   | (Sparkling air &amp; hooks)     | (Formant Vocal Chops) | Shimmering Plate Reverb |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.7 (Future Bass Architecture)","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-2","title":"13.7.2 — The 32-Voice Euphoric Supersaw","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.2 — The 32-Voice Euphoric Supersaw","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: 32-VOICE EUPHORIC SUPERSAW                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Unison: **16 Voices**   |\n|                      | Detune: **24%**, Blend: **75%**, Spread: **100%**      |\n|                      | Phase: **Random 100%** (Zero flanging on chords)       |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **OSCILLATOR 2**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Saw)**, Octave: **+1**          |\n|                      | Unison: **12 Voices**, Detune: **18%**, Level: **-4 dB**|\n|                      | Phase: **Random 100%**                                 |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **OSCILLATOR 3**     | Table: **Basic Shapes (Square)**, Octave: **-1**       |\n|                      | Unison: **4 Voices**, Detune: **10%**, Level: **-6 dB**|\n|                      | (Adds low-mid body and warmth)                         |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Analog LP24**, Cutoff: **14 kHz**, Res: **0.10**|\n|                      | Keytrack: **100%**                                     |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Compressor:** Mode **Multiband (OTT)**, Mix **65%**|\n|                      | 2. **Chorus:** Voices **4**, Mix **25%**               |\n|                      | 3. **Reverb:** Size **60%**, Decay **2.2 s**, Mix **22%**|\n|                      | 4. **Delay:** Ping-Pong (1/8th Dotted), Mix **18%**    |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **VOICING PANEL**    | **Polyphony: 8 Voices**                                |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A massive, shimmering, 32-voice composite supersaw chord engine that fills the entire stereo soundstage."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 2 &amp; 7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-3","title":"13.7.3 — The Rhythmic Pumping Chord LFO","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.3 — The Rhythmic Pumping Chord LFO","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The defining rhythmic movement of Future Bass (made famous by Flume and Illenium) is using an <strong>LFO to pump chord volume and filter cutoff</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ HELD 4-BAR SUPERSAW CHORD ] ===&gt; [ LFO 1: 1/4th Note Sawtooth Down Drop ]\n                                                  |\n                                                  +---&gt; Modulates Master Amp Volume (0% -&gt; 100%)\n                                                  +---&gt; Modulates Filter 1 Cutoff (400 Hz -&gt; 14 kHz)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">Amplitude / Cutoff\n 100% |      /|      /|      /|      /|\n   0% |--+---+---+---+---+---+---+---+---&gt; Time (1/4th Note Rhythmic Pumping Beat)</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Each quarter-note beat starts low and swells rapidly to maximum volume, creating an explosive, breathing chord progression."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.7.1"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-4","title":"13.7.4 — Pitch-Bend Scoop Onset Gestures","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.4 — Pitch-Bend Scoop Onset Gestures","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To add emotional human expression to chord changes:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ ENVELOPE 2 ] ===&gt; Attack: 0 ms, Decay: 55 ms, Sustain: 0.0\n                          |\n                          v\n          [ Route to OSC 1, 2, 3 PITCH (+12 Semitones) ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Every time a new chord is struck on the keyboard, the pitch instantly scoops upward from -1 octave into the true note pitch over 55 ms, creating the signature Future Bass melodic swell."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 5.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-5","title":"13.7.5 — The Bright Kawaii / Melodic Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.5 — The Bright Kawaii / Melodic Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| PATCH SPECIFICATION: BRIGHT KAWAII MELODIC PLUCK                              |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **SYNTH ENGINE**     | **Vital**                                              |\n| **OSCILLATOR 1**     | Table: **Square / Bell**, Octave: **+1**               |\n|                      | AEG 1: Attack **0 ms**, Decay **280 ms**, Sustain **0.0**|\n| **FILTER 1**         | Mode: **Comb+**, Cutoff: **2.2 kHz**, Feedback: **65%**|\n| **EFFECTS RACK**     | 1. **Delay:** Ping-Pong (1/8th Dotted, Mix: 25%)       |\n|                      | 2. **Reverb:** Size **75%**, Decay **3.0 s**, Mix **25%**|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A sparkling, crystalline melodic pluck that dances over heavy chord progressions."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Vital User Manual</em>, Section 2 &amp; 4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-6","title":"13.7.6 — Expressive Vocal Chop Lead","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.6 — Expressive Vocal Chop Lead","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">1. LOAD AN EMOTIONAL VOCAL PHRASE INTO SIMPLER (Slicing Mode).\n2. SET WARP TO COMPLEX PRO (Formant Preservation = 100%).\n3. TRANSPOSE UP +7 SEMITONES (+1 Fifth).\n4. SET AMP ENVELOPE: Attack 10 ms, Decay 400 ms, Sustain 0.50, Release 250 ms.\n5. INSERT DELAY (Ping-Pong 1/4th) AND LUSH REVERB (Decay 3.5 s).</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Result:</em> A soaring, emotive vocal synth lead that delivers the main melodic hook of the drop."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12 (Recipe E)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-7","title":"13.7.7 — Future Bass Chord Voicing Theory","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.7 — Future Bass Chord Voicing Theory","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Future Bass chords rely on extended jazz voicings:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| Chord Type       | Formula Intervals     | Musical Sound Design Character                     |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Major 7th**    | $1 - 3 - 5 - 7$       | Warm, nostalgic, emotional, uplifting.             |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Minor 9th**    | $1 - b3 - 5 - b7 - 9$ | Deep, melancholic, complex, lush.                  |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| **Add9 / Sus2**  | $1 - 2 - 3 - 5$       | Modern, open, shimmering stadium pop brilliance.   |\n+------------------+-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Open Voicing Spread:</strong> Spread notes across 3 octaves (Root in Octave 2, 5th in Octave 3, 3rd/7th/9th in Octave 4) to let the supersaw breathe without frequency clustering."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.7.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-8","title":"13.7.8 — The 808 Foundation Layer","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.8 — The 808 Foundation Layer","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ FUTURE BASS CHORD STACK ] ===&gt; [ HIGH-PASS FILTER (HP48 @ 100 Hz) ] ===&gt; (Mid Processing)\n                                                                                  +\n[ CLEAN 808 SUB TRACK     ] ===&gt; [ OPERATOR SINE @ 45 Hz ] ===&gt; [ UTILITY: MONO ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Rule:</strong> High-pass all supersaw chords at 100 Hz to eliminate phase clashes with the dedicated 808 sub track."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §12"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-9","title":"13.7.9 — Future Bass Drop Arrangement Grid","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.9 — Future Bass Drop Arrangement Grid","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">TRACK 1: Punchy Trap Kick   (Half-Time: Beat 1 and syncopated upbeat)\nTRACK 2: Heavy Trap Snare   (Beat 3 of every bar)\nTRACK 3: Gliding 808 Sub    (Mono, locked to chord roots)\nTRACK 4: Pumping Supersaws  (1/4-note and 1/8-note LFO pumping chords)\nTRACK 5: Kawaii Pluck Lead  (16th-note arpeggiated melodic motifs)\nTRACK 6: Pitched Vocal Chop (Main emotional drop hook)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 12.7.3"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-10","title":"13.7.10 — Future Bass Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.10 — Future Bass Macro Performance Rack","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                       FUTURE BASS LAUNCHKEY MACRO MAP                         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | **Supersaw Filter Cutoff (Dark Bed -&gt; Stadium Anthem)**   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 2**       | **LFO Pump Rate (1/4 -&gt; 1/8 -&gt; 1/16 -&gt; 1/32)**            |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 3**       | **Pitch-Scoop Onset Amount (0 st -&gt; +12 st)**             |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 4**       | **OTT Multiband Crunch Amount**                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 5**       | **Pluck Brightness &amp; Decay**                              |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 6**       | **Vocal Chop Reverb / Space Throw**                       |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 7**       | **Supersaw Unison Detune Spread**                         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Macro 8**       | **Master High-Pass Build Sweep**                          |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-11","title":"13.7.11 — Lab: Building a Complete 150 BPM Future Bass Drop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.11 — Lab: Building a Complete 150 BPM Future Bass Drop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Hands-On Milestone:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Set project tempo to 150 BPM (Half-time grid).","Construct a 32-voice supersaw chord patch in <code>Vital</code> with a 1/4-note LFO sidechain pump.","Program a 4-bar Major 7th / Minor 9th chord progression using open spreads.","Add a +12 semitone pitch-scoop attack envelope to the chords.","Synthesize a clean 808 sub in <code>Operator</code> following the chord root notes.","Program a half-time trap drum beat and layer a pitched vocal chop melody on top.","Export your complete Future Bass drop stem as <code>SD_Lab_FutureBassDrop_150BPM</code>."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §15"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-13-7-12","title":"13.7.12 — Gate J: Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"13.7.12 — Gate J: Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Before advancing to <strong>Module 14 (Systems, Performance Surface, Capstone)</strong>, verify your multi-genre sound design competencies:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             GATE J CHECKLIST                                  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| [ ] 1. Sub-Bass Separation Literacy:                                          |\n|     Can you explain why separating sub-bass (&lt;100 Hz mono sine) from mid-range|\n|     distorted growls and supersaw chords is mandatory across all EDM genres?  |\n|                                                                               |\n| [ ] 2. Dubstep / Bass Music Mastery:                                          |\n|     Can you synthesize a vocal formant growl in Vital and an FM growl in      |\n|     Operator from scratch in under 2 minutes?                                 |\n|                                                                               |\n| [ ] 3. Drum &amp; Bass Reese Construction:                                        |\n|     Can you synthesize both a classic 1995 Reese and a modern neurofunk       |\n|     notch-swept Reese with verified 20-cent phase beating?                   |\n|                                                                               |\n| [ ] 4. House &amp; UK Garage Execution:                                           |\n|     Can you synthesize a 1:2 FM donk bass and an additive drawbar organ stab   |\n|     in Operator and apply 58% swing in Live 12?                               |\n|                                                                               |\n| [ ] 5. Trap &amp; Future Bass Stacks:                                             |\n|     Can you build a gliding 808 sub with mono legato and a 32-voice pumping   |\n|     supersaw chord stack with pitch-scoop attack?                             |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"If all 5 criteria are verified by ear and manual execution, <strong>Gate J is passed</strong>. You have achieved total genre sound design fluency across all major electronic styles. Proceed to <strong>Module 14: Systems, Performance Surface, and Capstone</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound Design Foundations Syllabus</em>, §3 (Gate J Definition)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
